## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of SageMaker for anomaly detection, focusing on real-time latency requirements, data residency constraints, and phased deployment strategies using canary releases.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection models (Isolation Forest, autoencoders)
- Time-series feature engineering (rolling windows)
- Endpoint configuration and autoscaling (min/max instances, latency targets)
- Monitoring and drift detection (SageMaker Clarify, CloudWatch)
- Cost optimization and regional data compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "TrainingJobName": "anomaly-detection-train",
  "AlgorithmSpecification": { 
    "TrainingImage": "<isolation-forest-image>", 
    "TrainingInputMode": "File" 
  },
  "InputDataConfig": [{
    "ChannelName": "training",
    "DataSource": {
      "S3DataSource": {
        "S3DataType": "S3Prefix",
        "S3Uri": "s3://training-data/login-patterns/"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests building a low-latency, privacy-preserving NLP service with in-VPC explainability and PrivateLink access to a private data lake. It also probes rollout strategy and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Low-latency NLP inference on a small multilingual LM
- In-container explainability (Integrated Gradients) within a VPC
- PrivateLink access to data lake and Redis cache in VPC
- Canary rollouts with rollback on latency drift or metric drop
- Cost controls and autoscaling policies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-invocation of inference+explanation
async function inferWithExplain(input) {
  const pred = await callEndpoint(input);
  const expl = await callExplainService(input, pred);
  return { pred, expl };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test latency and explainability under burst load?
- What rollback criteria would you codify in the deployment pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical edge deployment, OTA rollout, and telemetry-driven governance for real-world industrial settings.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Edge Manager OTA workflow
- Canary and phased rollouts with rollback triggers
- Telemetry-driven monitoring (latency, errors, drift)
- Edge manifest versioning and cryptographic signing
- Cost governance and access control

